# Trained model artifacts.
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib
models/*.txt
models/*.onnx
models/*.h5
!models/.gitkeep
# ...EXCEPT the four shipped bundles. Render builds the image from this repo, so
# the models have to be IN it -- there is no artifact store to pull from. A
# bundle left ignored here is not a missing file at runtime, it is a FAILED
# BUILD: Dockerfile COPYs it by name, and Render's build context is the git
# clone. It builds fine locally, where the context is your working tree and the
# ignored file is sitting right there -- so this is a gap that only shows up on
# deploy. That is exactly how the 24h/48h bundles were missed.
#
# ~29 MB each, ~116 MB for all four. Well under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit,
# but note that every retrain adds another copy to history PERMANENTLY -- at
# four bundles that is now ~116 MB per retrain. If it becomes a problem, move to
# Git LFS or fetch them from a release asset at build time.
#
# The forecast service loads these two (Dockerfile):
#   2024        serves scored 2025 comparisons
#   2024_2025   serves 2026 onward
!models/forecast_model_2024.pkl
!models/forecast_model_2024_2025.pkl
# The lag service loads these two (Dockerfile.lag). SPLIT_SERVICES.md says why
# they are a separate deploy.
!models/forecast_model_24h.pkl
!models/forecast_model_48h.pkl


# Data -- raw CSVs are build-time only and must never be committed.
#
# NOTE `data/*`, not `data/`. Excluding the DIRECTORY stops git descending into
# it at all, so no `!data/external/...` negation below can ever fire. Excluding
# its CONTENTS leaves the directory walkable and the negation works.
data/*
*.csv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.db
*.sqlite3
# ...EXCEPT data/external/, which is NOT source data. It is the holiday
# calendar and site metadata, read at CALL TIME by forecast.calendar_lux, so
# the container cannot start without it. Both negations are needed: git will
# not descend into an excluded directory to find the files inside it.
!data/external/
!data/external/*.json
# ...and data/history/, for the same reason and with the same two-line shape.
# It is the recent-count snapshot the LAG service reads at call time to answer
# GET /forecast/{lead}h without a payload -- built by
# scripts/build_lag_history.py from actuals/, so derived rather than source.
#
# THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL. Render builds the image from this repo, so a file left
# ignored here is absent from the build context and `COPY data/history/` in
# Dockerfile.lag fails the BUILD -- not the request. Render then keeps the
# previous deploy serving, so the symptom is "my change did nothing" and a live
# service answering 405 on a route that exists in main. That is precisely how
# this was found. 3.6 MB across 264 files.
!data/history/
!data/history/*.json

